# Shared Context Protocol

Knowledge from each work block is captured as one file in `01-docs/context/lessons/`, next to
the project knowledge base that `global-context-builder` maintains in `01-docs/context/`, so
every agent (human or AI) can reuse it on the next task. In a repository that is not a QA
workspace (no `.qa-project`), use `docs/context/lessons/` instead.

## When to write a lesson (offer it, do not wait to be asked)

At the **end of a work block**, when any of these apply:

1. Shared test infrastructure changed: fixtures, config, API clients or types, the Playwright
   config, CI.
2. Three or more spec files were restructured or merged, or a new feature folder was added.
3. A new reusable pattern (fixture, helper, convention) was introduced that others should adopt.
4. A backend quirk, flaky behaviour or environment-only defect was found: a runtime-vs-spec
   mismatch, a rate limit, an ordering dependency.
5. Environment variables, setup steps or the onboarding flow changed.
6. A pull request was opened or merged that will be a reference point for later work.

Skip it for one-line fixes, formatting, typo-only changes, or when the user says "quick fix,
don't document".

## When starting a task

Before coding, read `01-docs/context/lessons/*.md` (newest first) and say which ones you are
using. If a relevant lesson is missing, say so. A lesson does not override the knowledge base
or a skill: where they disagree, flag the disagreement instead of picking one.

## File layout

- Path: `01-docs/context/lessons/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<short-kebab-slug>.md` (date first, so `ls` is
  chronological).
- One file per work block. Never edit an earlier file; write a new one that references it.

## Required structure

```markdown
# Lesson: <Title>

- **Branch:** <branch-name or "none">
- **Date:** YYYY-MM-DD
- **Area:** <paths or feature>

## 1. Objective
## 2. Key Decisions
## 3. Important Context
## 4. What Worked
## 5. What Didn't Work
## 6. Reusable Insights
## 7. Next Agent Guidance
```

Concise and specific; written for someone with no prior context; actionable before complete.
Include concrete file paths, test IDs, error codes and commands the next agent can paste. Never
put a token, a password or a customer's data in a lesson.
